es as well as anyone in the  league big time multiple effort guy  place can defend five positions so I  think that type of leadership and the  thing that I really admire and respect  about them  his his work ethic is really special I  think obviously you can't do the things  that he's done without a lot of talent  but it's his drive his intelligence in  his love of the game usually as guys  achieve things sometimes they let up  this guy's kept the hunger of a rookie  throughout his career and he wants to  get better and I think that type of  examples perfect for our team Tom  Thibodeau the coach of the Timberwolves  joining us here on the Rich Eisen show  would you agree with the assessment of  reading of the NBA room by Daryl Morey  the general manager of the Rockets that  we are in the midst of an arms race a  weapons race in the NBA that we haven't  seen based on how the Warriors have put  their team together yeah I think when  you study what's going on in the league  I would say that's probably pretty  accurate you know obviously everyone's  chasing Golden State and you look at  Cleveland they're doing the same and  then you know everyone else is you know  in the fight for to add to their team to  compete so that's what you try to do and  I think it starts by developing your own  young players and then of course you try  to acquire as many good players as you  can and then when players start looking  around and a lot of these players they  know each other from the all-star games  and shared agents and the Team USA so  they build relationships with each other  and then it leads to players joining up  with each other and then right before  free agency is when the most smoke needs  to be separated from fire certainly when  you're just days removed from a draft  and the smoke for a lot of people  looking at Minnesota is at Ricky Rubio  is on the block what can you tell us  about that is that true well now I think  you know if people always try sometimes  you don't know where it's coming from  could be coming from agents a lot of  times it's other teams that are trying  to create things create a market but  when you have good players people are  going to be interested in them and we  look at our team in totality and we know  obviously we have cap space and we feel  like we have a very attractive team and  I think free agents with what to look at  first is the type of money it'll be  available then next thing who are the  players are there and how will I fit in  with them  so that's what we're looking for where  the next step for us is the free agency  piece so how close are you you think  today Warriors coach well you know  you're talking about a team that is its  historic greatness so you know for us I  think we have to take it step by step  and I think they're a good team to study  wasn't long ago where they had 123 games  and they went step by step and of course  when you know it's like in the 40s and  then 51 and then they added Iguodala and  Bogut and guys like that dream on of  course and then once they started  playing great defense the the offense I  think has always been there and you can  never overlook what you know Klay and  Steph have made to that team over a long  period of time they win 73 games and  then they had Durant so I said a lot of  people are chasing them and but for us  it's you know we know we have to improve  defensively and that'll be the next big  step for us well it's no shock you coach  Tom Thibodeau have mentioned defense I  believe just off the top of my head no  fewer than four times in this  conversation so far and I want you to  track that rich well I'll do that well  and and because it's interesting because  I'm wondering and I'm asking somebody  who spent many years as the assistant to  the Jeff Van Gundy Knicks from 96 204 um  when I look at the Warriors team and I  see how many people in a copycat league  are trying to maybe outscore them do you  think there's a possible pendulum swing  back to the days where asses are put on  the floor by enforcer types in the  middle of the lane is there a  possibility that we see that in the  association Tom I think the new rules  you know you're not going to be able to  do that but I think what you can't lose  sight of is how great a defensive team  Golden State is so it's not only their  offense that you have to deal with you  have to deal with their defense but I  think the importance of defense is never  that's never changed if you went back  the last 20 years and you looked at the  conference final  you see they're well-balanced they're  strong on both sides of the ball  but I think you have to take a look at  some things that maybe outside of the  box  to try to you know at least slow Golden  State down some and I don't know if you  can do that that they that team is very  well put together I think you have to  try to make them work for their points  but they shoot the three from places  that you're not accustomed to defending  a step basically one dribble over  half-court and clay same thing that's a  good shot for those guys I had the  opportunity to coach them with Team USA  and they work on it and they showed them  and they make seven you know like I  think you have to be aware alert you  have to challenge you have to have a  multiple effort mentality and I think  the versatility I think the six eight  six nine guys six seven as many of those  guys as you can get that can defend I  think that's important and shoot threes  too I guess right I mean a two or three  because I mean you know the thing is  they're going to put forty threes up and  so if you're if they're making you know  eighteen or twenty and you're making six  that's it that's almost an impossible  deficit to make up no it is a beautiful  thing to watch right a team that passes  so much and the team that's so fluid in  offense and it's it really is a it is a  beautiful thing to watch but part of me  coach misses seeing coaches hanging on  to the ankles of Alonzo Mourning you  know when they're just getting out there  as I'm sure you know that you're talking  about the good old days yes but well is  there is there oh I know you mentioned  the rules but well the rules have  changed the game and I think for the  better it crossed over I mean we're  seeing great basketball but I think some  things probably do have to be tightened  up you know like where we've taken you  know the use of hands and and Chuck's  across the lane where that we've taken  that out and you know the hard files and  I think that's helped open up the game  but then I think if we're going to do  that  I think offensively we have to make sure  that you know we're not allowing players  to travel and carry carry the ball I  think we have to tighten it up there as  well so if you could wave your wand and  change a rule what would that be coach  Tom Thibodeau what could you do if I  gave you the if I give  the floor in front of the the Board of  Governors competition committee however  what do you do I think we you know the  the thing I don't like I think the the  scoring went up three points a game this  year and a lot of it has been the  free-throws I think a little more  clarity and there is going to there's  going to be some contact on every play  particularly on pick-and-rolls  like I hate the play in which the guy  comes off on a pick-and-roll and there's  contact and you know it's marginal at  best and it's an automatic you know the  players in our league are so smart they  figure out very quickly how the games  being called and I don't think any of us  want to see a game in which were you  know looking at 60 free-throws being  shot you know so I think they have to  let a little bit more go on on the  pick-and-roll coverage and just it you  know to tighten up the traveling I think  internationally our players in having  coached with the Olympics our player is  adept very well like I thought we would  be called for a lot of him we weren't  because they adjusted you know they got  the ball out of the hand before they  lifted the pivot foot and it was good  you know so I would say that probably  the you know to allow more contact  marginal contact on the pick and rolls  would that would be the first one the  second one is to tighten up on the  travel calls so by now coach do you  think Jimmy's changed his number or we  call it we had those girls out rich  looking for the we're outside but you're  absolutely going to call him up we have  is that we have his number but we have  an update that number is now unavailable  I was bad very fast oh my gosh you never  know right coaching this Danish you're  gonna hear SOT yeah I'll take my shot at  the title anyway we'll give it a try  coach thanks for calling really  appreciate having me always thank you  that's a coach Tom Thibodeau so Rich  Eisen show weekdays at noon eastern on  radio stations across the country and  audience  isn't it amazing you can download an app  with your thumbprint you should download  our app with your thumbprint

